# REST API Design Rules

## URL Conventions
- Base path: `/api/v1/`
- Plural nouns for collections: `/events`, `/bookings`, `/users`
- Kebab-case for multi-word segments: `/ticket-types`
- Nested routes only one level deep:
  - `/events/:id/bookings` ✓
  - `/events/:id/bookings/:bid/tickets` ✗ (too deep — use `/bookings/:bid`)

## HTTP Method Semantics
```
GET    /events              → list (paginated, filterable)
GET    /events/:id          → single resource
POST   /events              → create
PUT    /events/:id          → full replace (rare)
PATCH  /events/:id          → partial update (preferred)
DELETE /events/:id          → delete
POST   /events/:id/publish  → state transition (not PATCH)
POST   /events/:id/cancel   → state transition
```

## Route Map (complete)
```
# Auth (public)
POST   /api/v1/auth/register
POST   /api/v1/auth/login
POST   /api/v1/auth/refresh
POST   /api/v1/auth/logout

# Events (public browse)
GET    /api/v1/events                    ?page&size&category&title&from&to&minPrice&maxPrice&city
GET    /api/v1/events/:id
GET    /api/v1/events/recommended        (auth required)

# Events (organizer)
POST   /api/v1/events                    [organizer+]
PATCH  /api/v1/events/:id                [organizer, own event]
DELETE /api/v1/events/:id                [organizer, own event, before bookings]
POST   /api/v1/events/:id/publish        [organizer, own event]
POST   /api/v1/events/:id/cancel         [organizer, own event]
GET    /api/v1/events/:id/bookings       [organizer, own event]

# Ticket Types
POST   /api/v1/events/:id/ticket-types   [organizer]
PATCH  /api/v1/events/:id/ticket-types/:tid
DELETE /api/v1/events/:id/ticket-types/:tid

# Photos
POST   /api/v1/events/:id/photos         [organizer] multipart/form-data
DELETE /api/v1/events/:id/photos/:pid

# Bookings
POST   /api/v1/bookings                  [attendee+]
GET    /api/v1/bookings/my               [attendee+]
GET    /api/v1/bookings/:id              [attendee (own) or organizer (event owner)]

# Messaging
GET    /api/v1/messages/inbox            [auth]
GET    /api/v1/messages/sent             [auth]
GET    /api/v1/messages/unread-count     [auth]
POST   /api/v1/messages                  [auth]
DELETE /api/v1/messages/:id              [auth, own message]
GET    /api/v1/messages/events/:id/notify [SSE, auth] — unread notification stream

# Admin
GET    /api/v1/admin/users               [admin]
GET    /api/v1/admin/users/:id           [admin]
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/users/:id/approve   [admin]
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/users/:id/reject    [admin]
GET    /api/v1/admin/events/export/xml   [admin]
GET    /api/v1/admin/events/export/json  [admin]

# User profile
GET    /api/v1/users/me                  [auth]
PATCH  /api/v1/users/me                  [auth]
```

## Response Envelope
```json
// Success — single resource
{ "data": { "id": "...", "title": "..." }, "error": null }

// Success — collection
{
  "data": [...],
  "error": null,
  "meta": {
    "page": 1,
    "page_size": 10,
    "total": 243,
    "total_pages": 25
  }
}

// Error
{
  "data": null,
  "error": "event is not open for booking",
  "details": { "field": "validation message" }  // optional, for 422
}
```

## HTTP Status Codes
```
200 OK              → successful GET, PATCH, DELETE (with body)
201 Created         → successful POST (resource created)
204 No Content      → successful DELETE (no body)
400 Bad Request     → malformed JSON / missing required params
401 Unauthorized    → missing or invalid JWT
403 Forbidden       → authenticated but wrong role / not owner
404 Not Found       → resource doesn't exist
409 Conflict        → duplicate (username taken, etc.)
422 Unprocessable   → validation errors (field-level details)
429 Too Many Requests → rate limit hit
500 Internal Server Error → unexpected — never leak stack traces
```

## Filtering & Search Query Params
```
GET /api/v1/events
  ?page=1
  &size=10
  &category=Music
  &title=jazz           (partial match, case-insensitive)
  &q=free+text+search   (full-text via tsvector)
  &from=2025-07-01      (ISO 8601 date)
  &to=2025-12-31
  &min_price=0
  &max_price=50
  &city=Αθήνα
  &status=published     (default; admin can query others)
```

